===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having a [[fast]] [[pace]], [[tempo]], or [[beat]].
#: {{ux|en|The notes are easy, but it's an '''upbeat''' tune and should be played fairly quickly.}}
# Having a [[positive]], [[lively]], or [[perky]] [[tone]], [[attitude]], etc.
#: {{ux|en|Though he had bad news, he ended with an '''upbeat''' forecast for the future.}}
#: {{ux|en|He sounded '''upbeat''' when I talked to him.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 August 24|author=Steve Murphy tells Paul Stephen|title=Rail + property: a winning combination|journal=RAIL|issue=964|page=48|text=But Murphy remains '''upbeat''' about the longer-term prospect of recovery and a resumption of the record growth in passenger volumes experienced in the UK in the two decades following privatisation.}}

====Antonyms====
* {{antsense|optimistic}} {{l|en|downbeat}}

